## Bug fixed in /echo/middleware/proxy.go

### Root cause
- `randomBalancer.Next` called `b.random.Intn(len(b.targets))` → `panic: invalid argument to Intn` when `len(targets)==0`.
- `roundRobinBalancer.Next` did `b.i % uint32(len(b.targets))` → `panic: runtime error: integer divide by zero` when `len(targets)==0`.
- `ProxyWithConfig`'s handler dereferenced the returned target (`proxyHTTP(tgt, ...)`, `proxyRaw(tgt, ...)`), so a nil target would still crash.

### Exact diff (only file changed: /echo/middleware/proxy.go; 11 insertions, 0 deletions)
```diff
@@ -180,11 +180,19 @@ func (b *randomBalancer) Next(c echo.Context) *ProxyTarget {
 	}
 	b.mutex.RLock()
 	defer b.mutex.RUnlock()
+	if len(b.targets) == 0 {
+		return nil
+	}
 	return b.targets[b.random.Intn(len(b.targets))]
 }

 // Next returns an upstream target using round-robin technique.
 func (b *roundRobinBalancer) Next(c echo.Context) *ProxyTarget {
+	b.mutex.RLock()
+	defer b.mutex.RUnlock()
+	if len(b.targets) == 0 {
+		return nil
+	}
 	b.i = b.i % uint32(len(b.targets))
 	t := b.targets[b.i]
 	atomic.AddUint32(&b.i, 1)
@@ -229,6 +237,9 @@ func ProxyWithConfig(config ProxyConfig) echo.MiddlewareFunc {
 			req := c.Request()
 			res := c.Response()
 			tgt := config.Balancer.Next(c)
+			if tgt == nil {
+				return echo.ErrServiceUnavailable
+			}
 			c.Set(config.ContextKey, tgt)
```
Notes: `roundRobinBalancer.Next` now takes `b.mutex.RLock()` (the same `commonBalancer` RWMutex already used by `randomBalancer.Next`); no new lock ordering, no deadlock (Next never calls Add/RemoveTarget), and it removes the unsynchronized read of `b.targets`. `atomic.AddUint32(&b.i, 1)` is unchanged. `echo.ErrServiceUnavailable` = HTTP 503 (echo.go:281).

